---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import AccountabilitySurface from "../components/AccountabilitySurface.astro";
import { METRICS } from "../data/metrics";
const M = METRICS;
---
<Base title="FloodWatch.PH - where the model says it floods, but the record barely shows it" pathname="/">

  <!-- SPINE HERO. The recurrence-vs-record gap is the first thing, framed as
       step 1 of the accountability question. Server-rendered static text,
       present at first paint with no JavaScript. The numbers come from
       metrics.ts, never hardcoded prose. -->
  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 pt-12 pb-8">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-500 mb-4 font-mono">
      FloodWatch.PH &middot; the recurrence-vs-record gap
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[1.07] mb-5 text-ink-900 font-semibold tracking-tight max-w-3xl">
      Where the model says it floods, but the record barely shows it.
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mb-5 max-w-2xl">
      {M.uncharted_count} Philippine provinces are rated flood-prone by the
      recurrence model yet show few or no events in the historical observed
      record. That gap is step 1 of one accountability question: where does it
      repeatedly flood, so public flood-control spending can be held against it.
    </p>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-px bg-ink-300/40 border border-ink-300/40 max-w-2xl mb-6">
      <div class="bg-paper p-4">
        <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono mb-1">reproducible</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
          One repo, bit-exact, hash-verified. The recurrence model retrains in
          about 30 seconds on any laptop, no GPU.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-paper p-4">
        <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono mb-1">the class others skip</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
          The pluvial and urban flooding Google Flood Hub says it does not
          model. Observed after the fact, openly.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-paper p-4">
        <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono mb-1">private by build</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
          The area lookup runs in your browser. Your query is never sent,
          logged, or republished.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a
        href="/lookup"
        class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium no-underline bg-ink-900 text-white hover:bg-ink-700 transition-colors"
      >
        Check the gap for a place or a route
      </a>
      <a
        href="/map"
        class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium no-underline border border-ink-900 text-ink-900 hover:bg-ink-900 hover:text-white transition-colors"
      >
        Open the hazard-gap map
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 leading-relaxed mt-5 max-w-2xl">
      Open-source. CC-BY-4.0 data. No paywalls. Inputs are 100% public-licensed.
      <a href="/methodology" class="no-underline text-accent-steel">How the method works &rarr;</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- The gap, stated as the civic finding -->
  <section class="max-w-prose mx-auto px-6 py-10 border-t border-ink-300/30">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono mb-3">the finding</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl mb-4 leading-tight text-ink-900">Modeled-prone, thinly recorded.</h2>
    <p class="text-base text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Philippine communities flood repeatedly, yet the historical observed
      record is uneven. FloodWatch.PH measures the v1.0 gap: provinces the
      recurrence model (Track B) rates flood-prone but that appear with few or
      no events in the historical observed record (the Global Flood Database).
      The cross-reference against the official UP NOAH / PAGASA / MGB hazard
      maps is a v1.1 refinement, deferred because those government layers are
      token-gated or served only through single-page apps that cannot be
      fetched as data.
    </p>
    <p class="text-base text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Exposure and the modeled-vs-observed gap are aggregated to province (FAO
      GAUL level-2, ~82 Philippine provinces); city and barangay resolution is
      a v1.1 refinement.
    </p>
    <p class="text-base text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      Language throughout stays conservative. "Observed flood extent" and
      "warrants verification," not accusations. Output informs LGU disaster
      planning. <a href="/safety" class="no-underline text-accent-steel">Responsible use guide &rarr;</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Headline numbers -->
  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-10 grid gap-px bg-ink-300/40 md:grid-cols-4 border border-ink-300/40">
    <div class="bg-paper p-5">
      <div class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono">under-observed prone</div>
      <div class="font-mono tabular-nums text-2xl text-ink-900 mt-0.5">{M.uncharted_count}</div>
      <div class="text-[10px] text-ink-500 mt-0.5">provinces modeled-prone, under-observed</div>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-paper p-5">
      <div class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono">recurrence model F1</div>
      <div class="font-mono tabular-nums text-2xl text-ink-900 mt-0.5">{M.trackB_f1}</div>
      <div class="text-[10px] text-ink-500 mt-0.5">Track B, event-disjoint holdout</div>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-paper p-5">
      <div class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono">population exposed</div>
      <div class="font-mono tabular-nums text-2xl text-ink-900 mt-0.5">{M.pop_exposed}</div>
      <div class="text-[10px] text-ink-500 mt-0.5">WorldPop province aggregate, Carina peak</div>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-paper p-5">
      <div class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono">classifier sha256</div>
      <div class="font-mono tabular-nums text-2xl text-ink-900 mt-0.5">{M.clf_sha256}</div>
      <div class="text-[10px] text-ink-500 mt-0.5">bit-exact, hash-verified</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Two-track explanation -->
  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 pb-10 mt-4">
    <div class="grid gap-px bg-ink-300/40 md:grid-cols-2 border border-ink-300/40">
      <div class="bg-paper p-6 md:p-8">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono mb-2">Track B &middot; recurrence model</p>
        <h2 class="text-xl mb-2 text-ink-900">Which places flood repeatedly</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-3 leading-relaxed">
          Google AlphaEarth satellite embeddings (64-dim, 2017 annual) plus a logistic regression head trained on 57 Philippines GFD events (2002-2017). Event-disjoint holdout: entire typhoon events held out, never random pixels. Bit-exact, hash-verified, no GPU.
        </p>
        <p class="text-xs text-ink-500 font-mono">
          Track B holdout F1: <span class="text-ink-900">{M.trackB_f1}</span> &middot; Precision: <span class="text-ink-900">{M.trackB_precision}</span> &middot; Recall: <span class="text-ink-900">{M.trackB_recall}</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-paper p-6 md:p-8">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono mb-2">Track A &middot; event track</p>
        <h2 class="text-xl mb-2 text-ink-900">Observed flood extent from SAR</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-3 leading-relaxed">
          Sentinel-1 C-band SAR penetrates typhoon cloud cover. Each slider frame is a real acquisition date. Otsu threshold on the VH change image, permanent-water mask applied. Validated against the Global Flood Database (GFD) for Tropical Storm Koppu / Lando 2015 (event 4300).
        </p>
        <p class="text-xs text-ink-500 font-mono">
          Track A IoU vs GFD/CEMS (Koppu 2015): <span class="text-ink-900">{M.trackA_iou}</span> &middot; F1: <span class="text-ink-900">{M.trackA_f1}</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-ink-500 mt-2 leading-relaxed italic">
      Track A and Track B metrics are reported separately. They measure different things. The README never averages them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Accountability surface: the destination thesis as an in-progress
       roadmap line. Degrades gracefully when the wave B JSON is absent. -->
  <AccountabilitySurface variant="home" />

  <!-- D6: the observed-extent demo, demoted to a supporting section -->
  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-10 border-t border-ink-300/30">
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[1.4fr_1fr] gap-10 items-start">
      <div>
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono mb-3">supporting demonstration</p>
        <h2 class="text-2xl mb-3 text-ink-900 leading-tight">The observed substrate: where the water actually went.</h2>
        <p class="text-base text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
          The validated method (Koppu 2015, GFD event 4300) applied to the
          ungauged Super Typhoon Carina 2024 event, Metro Manila, 24 to 25 July
          2024. Carina had no promptly-public official flood-extent polygon;
          that absence is the civic vacuum this demonstration fills. A dated
          historical observation, not current conditions and not a forecast.
        </p>
        <a href="/map" class="text-sm font-medium text-accent-steel no-underline">Open the hazard-gap map and the 2024 demonstration &rarr;</a>
      </div>
      <aside class="border-l-2 border-ink-900 pl-5 text-sm text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="mb-2 font-mono text-xs text-ink-500 uppercase tracking-wider">what you get</p>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm">
          <li>Hazard gap: modeled-prone provinces under-observed in the historical record</li>
          <li>Track B recurrence model: which land signatures predict repeat flooding</li>
          <li>SAR-derived flood extent: time-slider across the Carina 2024 acquisition dates</li>
          <li>Province exposure: population, built-up area, peak flood share</li>
          <li>Permanent-water-masked: rivers and lakes removed, only flood reported</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Rainfall + expressway context: explicitly secondary, fully attributed.
       This is the one place realtime survives on the home page, below the
       spine, never the lead, never "freshest". -->
  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 pb-10">
    <div id="home-expressway" class="border border-ink-300/40 bg-paper-alt p-6 md:p-7">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono mb-2">
        rainfall + expressway context &middot; source: RainViewer / PAGASA, not produced by FloodWatch
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-lg mb-2 text-ink-900">Most recent observed pass, lagged</h2>
      <p id="home-expressway-line" class="text-sm text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        Checking the most recent observed satellite pass...
      </p>
      <p id="home-expressway-asof" class="text-xs text-ink-500 font-mono mb-3"></p>
      <a href="/map" class="text-sm font-medium text-accent-steel no-underline">Open the rainfall + expressway context tab &rarr;</a>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-ink-500 mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      Not a forecast. For live conditions, warnings, and routing during an
      active flood, use PAGASA (bagong.pagasa.dost.gov.ph), MMDA Flood Control,
      and your LGU DRRMO. FloodWatch is complementary to and never a replacement
      for these and Project NOAH / Google Flood Hub.
    </p>
  </section>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var lineEl = document.getElementById("home-expressway-line");
      var asOfEl = document.getElementById("home-expressway-asof");
      if (!lineEl) return;
      fetch("/data/road_flood_exposure.geojson")
        .then(function (r) { return r.ok ? r.json() : null; })
        .then(function (d) {
          var m = d && d._meta ? d._meta : null;
          if (!m) {
            lineEl.textContent =
              "The latest expressway-exposure layer is unavailable right now. Use MMDA Flood Control and PAGASA for live road conditions.";
            return;
          }
          var sum = m.expressway_summary || {};
          var names = Object.keys(sum);
          var flooded = 0, unknown = 0;
          for (var i = 0; i < names.length; i++) {
            flooded += sum[names[i]].flooded || 0;
            unknown += sum[names[i]].unknown || 0;
          }
          if (m.scan_status !== "ok") {
            lineEl.textContent =
              "The most recent Sentinel-1 pass was not usable, so expressway exposure could not be computed for this window. This is not a clear-conditions signal.";
          } else if (flooded === 0) {
            lineEl.textContent =
              "No monitored expressway segments (SLEX, NLEX, Skyway, CAVITEX, and the rest) intersect the most recent observed flood extent. This is the truthful current state of the latest pass, not an all-clear: the satellite has a ~6-day revisit with ~24 h product latency and conditions change between passes.";
          } else {
            lineEl.textContent =
              flooded + " monitored expressway segment" + (flooded === 1 ? "" : "s") +
              " intersected observed water on the latest pass. Observed, not a forecast or routing instruction.";
          }
          if (asOfEl && m.as_of) {
            asOfEl.textContent = "Observed pass as of " + m.as_of + " (Sentinel-1 ~6-day revisit, ~24 h product latency, not live). Rainfall context: RainViewer / PAGASA, not produced by FloodWatch.";
          }
        })
        .catch(function () {
          lineEl.textContent =
            "The latest expressway-exposure layer is unavailable right now. Use MMDA Flood Control and PAGASA for live road conditions.";
        });
    })();
  </script>

  <!-- Navigation cards -->
  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-10 grid gap-px bg-ink-300/40 md:grid-cols-2 border border-ink-300/40">
    <a href="/lookup" class="bg-paper p-6 md:p-8 no-underline group hover:bg-white transition-colors">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono mb-2">the spine, as a tool</p>
      <h2 class="text-xl mb-2 text-ink-900">Area &amp; route lookup</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Type a place or pick two points. FloodWatch states one conservative sentence on the recurrence-vs-record gap there, plus the dated evidence rows. Runs entirely in your browser; your query is never transmitted.
      </p>
      <span class="text-sm font-medium text-accent-steel group-hover:text-ink-900">Open the lookup &rarr;</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/methodology" class="bg-paper p-6 md:p-8 no-underline group hover:bg-white transition-colors">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono mb-2">how it works</p>
      <h2 class="text-xl mb-2 text-ink-900">Methodology</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Two-track architecture: Track B recurrence model (AlphaEarth embeddings + logistic regression, event-disjoint holdout), Track A SAR event detection (Otsu + permanent-water mask, parameter-free). Metrics reported separately, never averaged.
      </p>
      <span class="text-sm font-medium text-accent-steel group-hover:text-ink-900">Read methodology &rarr;</span>
    </a>
  </section>

  <p class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 pb-8 text-xs text-ink-500 leading-relaxed italic">
    Observed flood extent derived from public satellite data. Patterns may have legitimate explanations; figures warrant independent verification.
  </p>
</Base>
